ia the Cheeger constant. ... This approach works still on a compact finite-dimensional Alexandrov space of nonnegative curvature and proves affirmatively a conjecture of Funano and Shioya asserting a dimension free upper bound for eigenvalue ratios in that setting.\nTitle: An optimal dimension-free upper bound for eigenvalue ratios\nAuthors: Shiping Liu\nDate: Fri May  9 12:17:54 2014\n\nOn a closed weighted Riemannian manifold with nonnegative Bakry-\\'{E}mery Ricci curvature, it is shown that the ratio of the $k$-th to first eigenvalues of the weighted Laplacian is dominated by $641k^2$, using an argument via the Cheeger constant. While improving the previous exponential upper bound, the order of $k$ here is optimal, and hence answers an open question of Funano. This approach works still on a compact finite-dimensional Alexandrov space of nonnegative curvature and proves affirmatively a conjecture of Funano and Shioya asserting a dimension free upper bound for eigenvalue ratios in that setting.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n(PDF) An optimal dimension-free upper bound for eigenvalue ratios (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/262225425_An_optimal_dimension-free_upper_bound_for_eigenvalue_ratios)\nciteturn12search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 12.5 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; eigenvalue ratios was discovered by Funano-Shioya [13] through investigating ... 2 SHIPING LIU ... dimensional Alexandrov space of nonnegative curvature (see Conjecture 6.11 ... pecially whether this ratio can be dominated by a polynomial function of k ... Finally we remark that Theorem 1.3 is still true on a weighted Alexandrov\nwith multiplicity as below,\n\n0 = λ 0(M, µ)< λ 1(M , µ)≤λ 2(M, µ)≤ ··· ≤ λ k(M, µ)≤ · ·· ր ∞.\n\nWe prove the following theorem.\n\nTheorem 1.1. For any closed weighted Riemannian manifold (M , µ)of\n\nnonnegative Bakry- ´\n\nEmery Ricci curvature and any natural number k, we\n\nhave\n\nλ k(M, µ)≤16 e\n\ne